In application code, `StreamableValue` type from `ai/src` is reduced down to `{}` as a result of the tsconfig `stripInternal` option.

As mentioned [here](https://www.totaltypescript.com/the-empty-object-type-in-typescript),`{}` represents "any value except `null` and `undefined`", which makes the type essentially useless to import. It's also misleading because the type parameters aren't used anywhere in the resulting type, which means that `StreamableValue<string>` is equivalent to `StreamableValue<boolean>` in application code.

For example, in [examples/next-ai-rsc/app/stream-object-generate-itinerary.tsx](https://github.com/gclark-eightfold/ai/blob/0c408a3af027fd352f9ac52922d92bb85ea051cc/examples/next-ai-rsc/app/stream-object/generate-itinerary.tsx#L66-L72), if you make the following change, you will **not** get an error:
